{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-lagrangian-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:categorical-lagrangian-unique","kind":"proposition","title":"Uniqueness of the categorical Lagrangian","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-lagrangian-exists"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-lagrangian-unique"],"tags":["uniqueness","lagrangian"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalLagrangian.unique","text":"categorical-lagrangian-unique.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-lagrangian-unique.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:categorical-lagrangian-unique\"></a><p>For fixed <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\nabla, \\psi)</code>, the categorical Lagrangian <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}_q(\\nabla, \\psi)</code> is uniquely determined by its defining formula. Any endomorphism of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> equal to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{D}_\\nabla^2 + \\psi^* \\otimes \\mathcal{D}_\\nabla \\psi</code> coincides with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}_q</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-lagrangian-unique.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"3.12.3"}
